LEENIX focused Limine patch (v12.5.2).

LEENIX intentionally demotes these two Linux-loader progress messages to
verbose-only output so the LEENIUM menu remains visible while the
menu -> Plymouth transition stays clean.

- Normal boot (verbose=false): the two "linux: Loading ..." lines are hidden.
- VERBOSE=yes: they are shown again via printv().
- Panics, warnings, errors, menu rendering, timeout, editor policy, and boot
  semantics are untouched: only the two informational Linux x86 loader
  messages change from print() to printv().

